questions.question:
The tutor sent a 31-message chat with max_completion_tokens: 1000 and got:

400 {"error":{"code":"context_length_exceeded","message":"This model's maximum context length is 8192 tokens. However, you requested 8650 tokens (7650 in the messages, 1000 in the completion)."}}

Statement: "Sending the same 31 messages with max_completion_tokens: 500 would make this request fit the context window."

A second proposed fix for the tutor:

const messages = [{ role: "system", content: TUTOR_RULES }, ...chat];
while (countTokens(messages) > 7000) {
  messages.shift();          // drop the oldest message
}
const response = await client.chat.completions.create({ model, max_completion_tokens: 1000, messages });

Statement: "Because the system prompt is added before the chat, this loop removes only old chat turns and the tutor rules are always sent."
